            <ArticleTitle>[Characteristics of the peripheral neuromotor pathology in Chernobyl accident clean-up personnel late after the accident].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>18-20</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Clinical and electromyographic (EMG) examinations of the Chernobyl wreckers exposed to radiation revealed radiological damage to peripheral nervous system. 10-15 years after the accident they complain of weakness, headache, dizziness, muscle pain. Late damage to the peripheral nervous system manifest with EMG-detected axonal and demyelinating lesions, compression injuries of the peripheral nerves (tunnel syndromes), involvement of spinal cord motor neurons. In wreckers with thyroid lesions tunnel syndromes occur more often.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
